```java
public PriorityQueue(int initialCapacity, Comparator<? super E> comparator) {
    // Note: This restriction of at least one is not actually needed,
    // but continues for 1.5 compatibility
    if (initialCapacity < 1)
        throw new IllegalArgumentException();
    this.queue = new Object[initialCapacity];
    this.comparator = comparator;
    // @@@ If the initial capacity is greater than or equal to 1, then the size of the priority queue is 0.
}
```

Goal: assert that if initialCapacity >= 1, then size == 0 after construction. The method is a constructor, so we refer to this object's fields. Use this.size (field). The spec: initialCapacity >= 1 => this.size == 0.

